---
import Alternatives from '../../components/Alternatives.astro';
const faq = [
  { q: 'Does every Rella reviewer need a paid seat?', a: 'No. Rella prices creator/editor seats; external reviewers can use a share link without a paid seat. Pro offers public feedback links, Premium includes one assigned approver, and Premium Plus includes unlimited assigned approvers. Unlimited profiles does not mean unlimited editing seats.' },
  { q: 'Can the Rella MCP connector auto-post content?', a: 'The official Premium/Premium Plus connector can draft, schedule and manage workspace content, tasks, media and analytics, but its guide says it cannot enable auto-posting. Publication remains under the user’s control. Compare the exact action you need rather than assuming MCP implies unattended publishing.' },
  { q: 'How should I compare Rella AI costs?', a: 'Ella is not included on Pro. Premium has monthly credits and optional paid overage; Premium Plus advertises unlimited usage subject to fair use. The connector guide says external assistant use does not consume Ella credits. Include any assistant-provider bill separately.' },
];
const links = [
  { href: '/alternatives', label: 'All scheduler alternatives' },
  { href: '/alternatives/coschedule', label: 'CoSchedule alternatives: coordination versus publishing' },
  { href: '/docs/approvals', label: 'PostDelegate client review and approvals' },
  { href: '/docs/mcp', label: 'PostDelegate MCP and assistant costs' },
  { href: '/docs/channels/coming-soon', label: 'Networks waiting on approval' },
];
---
<Alternatives
  subject="rella" alternatives={['planable', 'buffer', 'publer', 'metricool']} published="2026-11-15"
  title="Rella Alternatives: Creator Seats, Review and Publishing"
  description="Compare Rella alternatives by paid creators, free reviewers, approval stages and publishing needs. Check MCP controls and AI costs before changing workflows."
  h1="Rella alternatives for creator seats, review and publishing"
  shortAnswer="Compare Planable for structured content review, Buffer for a smaller queue, Publer for publishing automation, and Metricool for reporting across brands. Stay with Rella when its tasks, Social Spaces and free external review already remove production handoffs."
  fitIntro="PostDelegate is our product. Compare it when your priority is publishing with an assistant or API, client approval links and a channel-based plan. Its live network coverage must fit first; a publishing workflow is not a verified replacement for every Rella task or production board."
  faq={faq} links={links}
>
  <Fragment slot="before-table">
    <h2>Count creators separately from reviewers</h2>
    <p>Rella's seat price is only meaningful after you identify who actually creates or edits content. Its <a href="https://getrella.com/pricing">pricing page</a> includes unlimited social profiles and Social Spaces, while external reviewers do not need paid seats. A business with many brands and few creators has a different cost shape from a business with many editors and a few profiles. Unlimited profiles is not a promise of unlimited editing users.</p>
    <p>Review depth also changes by tier. Pro has public feedback links but no assigned approvers. Premium includes one assigned approver, while Premium Plus includes unlimited assigned approvers and white labeling. Decide whether you need informal feedback, a named sign-off or a more extensive production process before comparing subscriptions. Tasks and approvals are part of the work, not incidental extras to a calendar.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Four alternatives to evaluate by role</h2>
  <h3>Planable: workspace cost instead of creator seats</h3>
  <p><a href="https://planable.io/pricing/">Planable's paid plans</a> include unlimited users, with limits per workspace on social pages and posts. Basic has optional approvals, Pro required approvals and Enterprise multi-level approvals. It is worth comparing when many people edit a relatively concentrated set of brands. Include the workspace count and any analytics, inbox or listening add-ons; unlimited users alone does not describe the total bill.</p>
  <h3>Buffer: a queue for a smaller publishing operation</h3>
  <p><a href="https://buffer.com/pricing">Buffer</a> starts with three free channels, one user and ten queued posts per channel. Team includes unlimited users and approval workflows. Consider it when the material is already prepared and the remaining job is scheduling and review. Before moving, identify where task assignments and production handoffs will live so that simplifying the queue does not scatter the rest of the work.</p>
  <h3>Publer: compare automation and additional members</h3>
  <p><a href="https://publer.com/help/en/article/what-are-publers-plans-and-pricing-15h4yqh/">Publer</a> prices selected social accounts plus additional members, with the owner included. Professional includes RSS and bulk scheduling; Business adds automatic recycling and recurring posts. Model the creators who need access separately from account count. Rella evergreen recycling was not established by the documentation checked here, which is a reason to verify your requirements, not to declare a missing feature.</p>
  <h3>Metricool: reporting and brand boundaries</h3>
  <p><a href="https://metricool.com/pricing/">Metricool</a> organizes one profile per network within each brand. Advanced adds team access and API access. It is a useful candidate when comparing performance across brands matters more than production boards. Check which people need access to which brands, and remember that connected websites or ad accounts do not imply social publishing to those destinations.</p>

  <h2>Compare assistant actions and AI bills separately</h2>
  <p>Rella already offers an <a href="https://support.getrella.com/articles/2582931593-rella-connector-guide">MCP connector on Premium and Premium Plus</a> for drafts, scheduling, tasks, media and analytics. The guide says it cannot enable auto-posting; publication stays under the user's control. It also says external assistant use does not consume Ella credits. Moving solely to obtain MCP could therefore solve a problem you do not have.</p>
  <p><a href="https://getrella.com/pricing">Ella availability</a> differs: Pro does not include it, Premium uses monthly credits with optional paid overage, and Premium Plus advertises unlimited usage subject to the <a href="https://getrella.com/fair-use-policy">fair-use policy</a>. The monthly seat figures in the table come from Rella's <a href="https://getrella.com/blog/rella-pricing-explained-which-plan-is-right-for-your-social-media-team">official guide labeled October 2026</a>; current pricing agrees on annual rates. No checkout or billing-toggle test was performed.</p>

  <h2>When staying with Rella makes sense</h2>
  <p>Keep Rella if its tasks, brand-specific Social Spaces and external review links already shorten the route from an idea to an approved post. Many brands managed by a small creator group may fit its pricing well. Public API endpoint details and plan entitlement were not established by the checked integration documentation; that uncertainty should prompt a precise integration check, not a claim that Rella has no API.</p>

  <h2>A production-workflow migration checklist</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Count paid creators/editors separately from people who only review through a link.</li>
    <li>Map Social Spaces, tasks, assets and assigned approvers to their new locations and permissions.</li>
    <li>Check every required network and account type, then validate a sample draft through review and scheduling.</li>
    <li>Compare Ella credits, external assistant charges and the publication action you need; preserve a reference copy of unfinished work.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>PostDelegate's <a href="/docs/approvals">client approval links</a> and agent controls are documented separately. Check <a href="/docs/channels/coming-soon">network availability</a> before considering a move: Facebook, Instagram, Threads, TikTok, LinkedIn company Pages and Pinterest are waiting on approval; X is unavailable. This page reflects public-source research, not first-hand testing or a verified transfer of Rella projects.</p>
</Alternatives>
